	'ip_about_s1_h' => 'Founded in 2014 from two neighbouring farmhouses',
	'ip_about_s1_p' => 'The Japanese word azukari refers to something placed in trust for someone else. In 2014, Maren Holt had managed housekeeping for a country hotel for 12 years, and Idris Calloway was working as an architectural photographer. When two neighbouring farm owners moved abroad and needed someone local to hold keys, manage changeovers, and answer late-night maintenance calls, Maren and Idris stepped in. That hands-on experience shaped our philosophy: owners living elsewhere need absolute reliability, pristine housekeeping, responsive guest communication, and transparent monthly financial accounting.',
	'ip_about_s2_h' => 'The seven people who look after your house',
	'ip_about_s3_h' => 'Our central operations at Corn Exchange Yard',
	'ip_about_s3_p' => 'Our headquarters at 14 Corn Exchange Yard in Lenning houses our central office, laundry, and equipment store. By running our own laundry facility with hotel-weight cotton, we maintain pristine bedding without depending on commercial third-party laundries. We strictly limit our intake to at most eight new properties per season across our six regions. We never promise inflated occupancy figures or fixed income claims, we charge no commission on guest cleaning fees, and we ensure that every house remains as well kept as the day we took the keys.',
	'ip_about_sub' => 'A holiday-let manager that started with two farmhouses and a key left on the kitchen table.',
	'ip_consult_bar_btn' => 'Request a time',
