	'tpl_archive_label' => 'Journal',
	'why_cap' => 'Lucía’s team hangs the Weller farmhouse linen to air before the 14:00 guests.',
	'why_h' => 'Two farmhouses, two neighbours abroad, and a key left with us.',
	'why_label' => 'About us · since 2014',
	'why_p1' => 'In 2014, Maren Holt and Idris Calloway took on two stone farmhouses in the Ostervale hills for neighbours who had moved abroad. The owners simply needed someone local who could be trusted with the keys, manage turnovers, and handle the unexpected 23:00 phone call about a boiler.',
	'why_p2' => 'Owners who live elsewhere need three things above all: one reliable person who always answers, a house that feels precisely the same each time they return, and plain numbers they can read at a glance. We look after holiday lets with the steady care of caretakers, ensuring every changeover preserves the property.',
	'why_p3' => 'What we do not do is just as important. We make no speculative promises or income forecasts, we never pack calendars with back-to-back stays that exhaust a house, and we accept at most eight new homes each season so our housekeeping and maintenance teams never lose their attention to detail.',
);
